    "title": "API and data model",
    "body": "**API:** `POST /links {longUrl}` returns `{code}`; `PATCH /links/{code}` changes the destination; `GET /{code}` answers with a redirect whose `Location` header holds the long link. **Data model:** `links(code primary key, long_url, owner, created_at)`, sharded by code (SD 8), and a click count per link and day. A redirect is one lookup by primary key, the cheapest query a database has.",
