  {
    "title": "Catching collisions",
    "body": "The server picks 7 random base62 characters, such as `aZ3kQ9x`, and inserts the row. Near the end of 5 years, 6 billion of 3.5 trillion codes are taken, so a new code repeats an old one about **1 time in 580**. Over 6 billion creations that happens millions of times, so it must be caught. The **unique primary key** makes the database reject the second insert, and the server simply tries a new code. Checking \"is it free?\" first and inserting later would let two servers take the same code between the steps.",
