  {
    "title": "301 or 302?",
    "body": "A **301** tells the browser the link moved for good, so the browser may keep the answer and go straight to the long link next time. The team then never sees those clicks, and if the destination changes, returning visitors still go to the **old page**. A **302** is temporary: the browser asks again each time. Here the team needs click counts and changes, so redirects use 302 with `Cache-Control: max-age=0, s-maxage=60`: browsers ask every time, and only the CDN may keep the answer for 60 seconds.",
