  {
    "title": "Fast redirects",
    "body": "A few links get most clicks. The CDN answers repeated clicks for up to 60 seconds; the app servers keep popular links in a **link cache** whose entries expire within 4 minutes, so a change shows within 5 minutes. Most of the 20,000 redirects per second never reach the database, and a cached lookup takes about a millisecond, well within 50 ms. Each redirect that reaches the servers sends a click event to a queue, counted in batches, and the CDN's own logs add the clicks it answered.",
