  {
    "title": "Failures and summary",
    "body": "**If the database's main copy fails**, redirects continue from the cache and a read replica (SD 6), while creations wait for failover. **If the link cache is lost**, the replicas carry the redirects until it refills. **A hot link** is answered mostly by the CDN. **Summary:** F1 by random codes; N3 by the unique key; F2 and N2 by cached key lookups; F3 by 302 with short cache times; F4 by click events counted in batches.",
